{"id":"tomar","es":"tomar","en":["to take","to drink"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"In Colombia the everyday verb for drinks: ¿qué vas a tomar? Also for transport: tomar un taxi.","sent":{"es":"Voy a {tomar} un taxi al aeropuerto.","en":"I am going to take a taxi to the airport."}}
{"id":"llamar","es":"llamar","en":["to call","to phone"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Both to phone someone and to call out to them.","sent":{"es":"Te {llamo} esta noche.","en":"I will call you tonight."}}
{"id":"llamarse","es":"llamarse","en":["to be called"],"pos":"verb","topic":"smalltalk","note":"How names work: me llamo Ana is literally I call myself Ana.","sent":{"es":"Mi perro se {llama} Max.","en":"My dog is called Max."}}
{"id":"conocer","es":"conocer","en":["to know","to meet"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"For people and places. saber is for facts. First person conozco. In the past, conocí means I met.","sent":{"es":"¿{Conoces} a mi hermana?","en":"Do you know my sister?"}}
{"id":"entrar","es":"entrar","en":["to go in","to come in","to enter"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"entrar a in Latin America, entrar en in Spain.","sent":{"es":"¿Podemos {entrar}?","en":"Can we come in?"}}
{"id":"subir","es":"subir","en":["to go up","to get on"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Also to get on a bus and to upload a photo.","sent":{"es":"Hay que {subir} las escaleras.","en":"You have to go up the stairs."}}
{"id":"bajar","es":"bajar","en":["to go down","to get off"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Also to get off a bus, and to download.","sent":{"es":"Me {bajo} en la próxima parada.","en":"I am getting off at the next stop."}}
{"id":"mostrar","es":"mostrar","en":["to show"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: muestro, muestras. enseñar also means to show.","sent":{"es":"¿Me {muestras} las fotos?","en":"Will you show me the photos?"}}
{"id":"explicar","es":"explicar","en":["to explain"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","sent":{"es":"¿Me lo puedes {explicar} otra vez?","en":"Can you explain it to me again?"}}
{"id":"ensenar","es":"enseñar","en":["to teach"],"pos":"verb","topic":"work","note":"Also to show: te enseño la casa.","sent":{"es":"Ella {enseña} inglés en un colegio.","en":"She teaches English at a school."}}
{"id":"recibir","es":"recibir","en":["to receive"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","sent":{"es":"{Recibí} tu mensaje.","en":"I received your message."}}
{"id":"cuidar","es":"cuidar","en":["to look after","to take care of"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"cuídate is take care.","sent":{"es":"¿Puedes {cuidar} a mi perro el fin de semana?","en":"Can you look after my dog at the weekend?"}}
{"id":"limpiar","es":"limpiar","en":["to clean"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","sent":{"es":"Tengo que {limpiar} la casa.","en":"I have to clean the house."}}
{"id":"lavar","es":"lavar","en":["to wash"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","note":"lavarse for washing yourself: lavarse las manos.","sent":{"es":"Voy a {lavar} la ropa.","en":"I am going to wash the clothes."}}
{"id":"cantar","es":"cantar","en":["to sing"],"pos":"verb","topic":"leisure","sent":{"es":"Ella {canta} muy bien.","en":"She sings very well."}}
{"id":"bailar","es":"bailar","en":["to dance"],"pos":"verb","topic":"leisure","note":"In Cali, the salsa capital, expect to be asked.","sent":{"es":"¿Quieres {bailar}?","en":"Do you want to dance?"}}
{"id":"nadar","es":"nadar","en":["to swim"],"pos":"verb","topic":"leisure","sent":{"es":"No sé {nadar}.","en":"I cannot swim."}}
{"id":"descansar","es":"descansar","en":["to rest"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"que descanses is sleep well.","sent":{"es":"Necesito {descansar} un rato.","en":"I need to rest for a while."}}
{"id":"despertarse","es":"despertarse","en":["to wake up"],"pos":"verb","topic":"routine","note":"Stem changes: me despierto. Without se it is to wake someone else.","sent":{"es":"Me {despierto} a las seis.","en":"I wake up at six."}}
{"id":"levantarse","es":"levantarse","en":["to get up"],"pos":"verb","topic":"routine","note":"Without se, levantar is to lift.","sent":{"es":"Me {levanto} temprano los lunes.","en":"I get up early on Mondays."}}
{"id":"ducharse","es":"ducharse","en":["to shower","to have a shower"],"pos":"verb","topic":"routine","note":"Colombians often say bañarse instead.","sent":{"es":"Me {ducho} por la mañana.","en":"I have a shower in the morning."}}
{"id":"vestirse","es":"vestirse","en":["to get dressed"],"pos":"verb","topic":"routine","note":"Stem changes: me visto.","sent":{"es":"Me {visto} y salgo.","en":"I get dressed and go out."}}
{"id":"acostarse","es":"acostarse","en":["to go to bed"],"pos":"verb","topic":"routine","note":"Stem changes: me acuesto.","sent":{"es":"Me {acuesto} a las once.","en":"I go to bed at eleven."}}
{"id":"sentarse","es":"sentarse","en":["to sit down"],"pos":"verb","topic":"routine","note":"Stem changes: me siento, which is also I feel. siéntese is the polite sit down.","sent":{"es":"¿Me puedo {sentar} aquí?","en":"Can I sit here?"}}
{"id":"preparar","es":"preparar","en":["to prepare"],"pos":"verb","topic":"food","note":"For meals: preparar la cena.","sent":{"es":"Voy a {preparar} la cena.","en":"I am going to make dinner."}}
{"id":"cortar","es":"cortar","en":["to cut"],"pos":"verb","topic":"food","note":"cortarse el pelo is to have your hair cut.","sent":{"es":"{Corta} el pan, por favor.","en":"Cut the bread, please."}}
{"id":"gastar","es":"gastar","en":["to spend"],"pos":"verb","topic":"paying","note":"For money. Spending time is pasar.","sent":{"es":"{Gasté} mucha plata en el viaje.","en":"I spent a lot of money on the trip."}}
{"id":"ahorrar","es":"ahorrar","en":["to save"],"pos":"verb","topic":"paying","note":"For money and time. Saving a life or a file is salvar or guardar.","sent":{"es":"Quiero {ahorrar} para el viaje.","en":"I want to save for the trip."}}
{"id":"nacer","es":"nacer","en":["to be born"],"pos":"verb","topic":"people","note":"An active verb in Spanish: nací, I was born.","sent":{"es":"{Nací} en Inglaterra.","en":"I was born in England."}}
{"id":"morir","es":"morir","en":["to die"],"pos":"verb","topic":"people","note":"Stem changes: muere, murió.","sent":{"es":"Mi abuelo {murió} el año pasado.","en":"My grandfather died last year."}}
{"id":"crecer","es":"crecer","en":["to grow","to grow up"],"pos":"verb","topic":"people","note":"First person crezco.","sent":{"es":"{Crecí} en un pueblo pequeño.","en":"I grew up in a small town."}}
{"id":"parar","es":"parar","en":["to stop"],"pos":"verb","topic":"travel","note":"For a bus or a car. To stop doing something is dejar de.","sent":{"es":"¿El bus {para} aquí?","en":"Does the bus stop here?"}}
{"id":"caer","es":"caer","en":["to fall"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Usually caerse: me caí, I fell over. First person caigo.","sent":{"es":"Cuidado, te vas a {caer}.","en":"Careful, you are going to fall."}}
{"id":"romper","es":"romper","en":["to break"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"The participle is irregular: roto, broken.","sent":{"es":"{Rompí} un vaso.","en":"I broke a glass."}}
{"id":"arreglar","es":"arreglar","en":["to fix","to sort out"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","sent":{"es":"¿Puedes {arreglar} la ducha?","en":"Can you fix the shower?"}}
{"id":"importar","es":"importar","en":["to matter"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Works like gustar: me importa, it matters to me. no importa is never mind.","sent":{"es":"No {importa}.","en":"It does not matter."}}
{"id":"encantar","es":"encantar","en":["to love"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"For things you love, working like gustar: me encanta. For people, use querer.","sent":{"es":"Me {encanta} esta canción.","en":"I love this song."}}
{"id":"molestar","es":"molestar","en":["to bother"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"Works like gustar: ¿te molesta? is do you mind?","sent":{"es":"¿Te {molesta} si abro la ventana?","en":"Do you mind if I open the window?"}}
{"id":"interesar","es":"interesar","en":["to interest"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"Works like gustar: me interesa, I am interested.","sent":{"es":"Me {interesa} mucho la historia.","en":"I am very interested in history."}}
{"id":"faltar","es":"faltar","en":["to be missing","to be short of"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Works like gustar: me falta plata, I am short of money.","sent":{"es":"{Falta} un tenedor.","en":"There is a fork missing."}}
{"id":"significar","es":"significar","en":["to mean"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"For words. For people meaning something, querer decir.","sent":{"es":"¿Qué {significa} esta palabra?","en":"What does this word mean?"}}
{"id":"suponer","es":"suponer","en":["to suppose"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Conjugates like poner: supongo.","sent":{"es":"{Supongo} que sí.","en":"I suppose so."}}
{"id":"ocurrir","es":"ocurrir","en":["to happen","to occur"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"pasar is the everyday version.","sent":{"es":"¿Qué {ocurrió} anoche?","en":"What happened last night?"}}
{"id":"decidir","es":"decidir","en":["to decide"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","sent":{"es":"No puedo {decidir}.","en":"I cannot decide."}}
{"id":"elegir","es":"elegir","en":["to choose"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem and spelling change: elijo, eliges.","sent":{"es":"Puedes {elegir} el restaurante.","en":"You can choose the restaurant."}}
{"id":"permitir","es":"permitir","en":["to allow"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"no se permite is not allowed.","sent":{"es":"No se {permite} fumar aquí.","en":"Smoking is not allowed here."}}
{"id":"prometer","es":"prometer","en":["to promise"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","sent":{"es":"Te lo {prometo}.","en":"I promise."}}
{"id":"confiar","es":"confiar","en":["to trust"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"Takes en: confío en ti.","sent":{"es":"{Confío} en ti.","en":"I trust you."}}
{"id":"mentir","es":"mentir","en":["to lie"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: miento. A lie is una mentira.","sent":{"es":"No me {mientas}.","en":"Do not lie to me."}}
{"id":"perdonar","es":"perdonar","en":["to forgive"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"perdona or perdone also does for excuse me.","sent":{"es":"¿Me {perdonas}?","en":"Will you forgive me?"}}
{"id":"agradecer","es":"agradecer","en":["to thank","to be grateful for"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"First person agradezco. te lo agradezco is I really appreciate it.","sent":{"es":"Te lo {agradezco} mucho.","en":"I really appreciate it."}}
{"id":"amar","es":"amar","en":["to love"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"Strong and romantic: te amo. Between friends and family, te quiero is the everyday one.","sent":{"es":"Te {amo}.","en":"I love you."}}
{"id":"abrazar","es":"abrazar","en":["to hug"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"un abrazo is a hug, and a common way to sign off a message.","sent":{"es":"Ven, te quiero {abrazar}.","en":"Come here, I want to hug you."}}
{"id":"casarse","es":"casarse","en":["to get married"],"pos":"verb","topic":"people","note":"casarse con, to marry someone.","sent":{"es":"Nos {casamos} en junio.","en":"We are getting married in June."}}
{"id":"manejar","es":"manejar","en":["to drive"],"pos":"verb","topic":"travel","note":"The Latin American word. Spain says conducir.","sent":{"es":"¿Sabes {manejar}?","en":"Can you drive?"}}
{"id":"reservar","es":"reservar","en":["to book","to reserve"],"pos":"verb","topic":"travel","sent":{"es":"Quiero {reservar} una mesa para dos.","en":"I would like to book a table for two."}}
{"id":"llenar","es":"llenar","en":["to fill","to fill in"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Also for forms: llenar un formulario.","sent":{"es":"Hay que {llenar} este formulario.","en":"You have to fill in this form."}}
{"id":"apagar","es":"apagar","en":["to turn off","to switch off"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","sent":{"es":"{Apaga} la luz, por favor.","en":"Turn off the light, please."}}
{"id":"prender","es":"prender","en":["to turn on","to switch on"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","note":"The Colombian word. Spain says encender.","sent":{"es":"¿Puedes {prender} el ventilador?","en":"Can you turn on the fan?"}}
{"id":"cargar","es":"cargar","en":["to charge"],"pos":"verb","topic":"tech","note":"Both charging a phone and carrying something heavy.","sent":{"es":"Necesito {cargar} el celular.","en":"I need to charge my phone."}}
{"id":"contar","es":"contar","en":["to count","to tell"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: cuento. To tell a story or news, rather than to say.","sent":{"es":"Te voy a {contar} un secreto.","en":"I am going to tell you a secret."}}
{"id":"mover","es":"mover","en":["to move"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: muevo. Moving house is mudarse.","sent":{"es":"¿Me ayudas a {mover} la mesa?","en":"Will you help me move the table?"}}
{"id":"mudarse","es":"mudarse","en":["to move house"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","sent":{"es":"Nos {mudamos} el mes pasado.","en":"We moved house last month."}}
{"id":"probar","es":"probar","en":["to try","to taste"],"pos":"verb","topic":"food","note":"For tasting food or trying something on. Trying hard to do something is intentar.","sent":{"es":"¿Quieres {probar} la sopa?","en":"Do you want to try the soup?"}}
{"id":"lograr","es":"lograr","en":["to manage","to achieve"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"lograr hacer algo, to manage to do something.","sent":{"es":"Por fin lo {logré}.","en":"I finally managed it."}}
{"id":"cumplir","es":"cumplir","en":["to turn","to keep"],"pos":"verb","topic":"time","note":"For birthdays, cumplir años. Also keeping a promise.","sent":{"es":"Mañana {cumplo} veinticinco años.","en":"Tomorrow I turn twenty-five."}}
{"id":"quitar","es":"quitar","en":["to take off","to remove"],"pos":"verb","topic":"clothes","note":"quitarse for your own clothes: quítate los zapatos.","sent":{"es":"{Quítate} los zapatos, por favor.","en":"Take your shoes off, please."}}
{"id":"sacar","es":"sacar","en":["to take out"],"pos":"verb","topic":"home","note":"Also to get money out, and to take a photo: sacar una foto.","sent":{"es":"Voy a {sacar} la basura.","en":"I am going to take the rubbish out."}}
{"id":"devolver","es":"devolver","en":["to give back"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: devuelvo.","sent":{"es":"Te {devuelvo} el libro mañana.","en":"I will give you the book back tomorrow."}}
{"id":"regresar","es":"regresar","en":["to come back","to go back"],"pos":"verb","topic":"travel","note":"Very Latin American; volver means the same.","sent":{"es":"¿A qué hora {regresas}?","en":"What time are you coming back?"}}
{"id":"depender","es":"depender","en":["to depend"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"depende on its own is it depends.","sent":{"es":"{Depende} del precio.","en":"It depends on the price."}}
{"id":"oir","es":"oír","en":["to hear"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Irregular: oigo, oyes, oye. escuchar is to listen.","sent":{"es":"No te {oigo} bien.","en":"I cannot hear you well."}}
{"id":"saludar","es":"saludar","en":["to greet","to say hello"],"pos":"verb","topic":"smalltalk","note":"saludos is regards, at the end of a message.","sent":{"es":"{Saluda} a tu mamá de mi parte.","en":"Say hello to your mum from me."}}
{"id":"visitar","es":"visitar","en":["to visit"],"pos":"verb","topic":"travel","sent":{"es":"Quiero {visitar} Cartagena.","en":"I want to visit Cartagena."}}
{"id":"invitar","es":"invitar","en":["to invite","to treat"],"pos":"verb","topic":"smalltalk","note":"yo invito means I am paying.","sent":{"es":"Yo te {invito} a un tinto.","en":"I will buy you a coffee."}}
{"id":"compartir","es":"compartir","en":["to share"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","sent":{"es":"¿Quieres {compartir} un taxi?","en":"Do you want to share a taxi?"}}
{"id":"fumar","es":"fumar","en":["to smoke"],"pos":"verb","topic":"body","sent":{"es":"No {fumo}.","en":"I do not smoke."}}
{"id":"llover","es":"llover","en":["to rain"],"pos":"verb","topic":"nature","note":"Stem changes: llueve.","sent":{"es":"Está {lloviendo} otra vez.","en":"It is raining again."}}
{"id":"quejarse","es":"quejarse","en":["to complain"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","sent":{"es":"Siempre se {queja} del tráfico.","en":"He always complains about the traffic."}}
{"id":"mejorar","es":"mejorar","en":["to improve","to get better"],"pos":"verb","topic":"body","note":"que te mejores is get well soon.","sent":{"es":"Mi español está {mejorando}.","en":"My Spanish is getting better."}}
{"id":"preferir","es":"preferir","en":["to prefer"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: prefiero.","sent":{"es":"{Prefiero} el café sin azúcar.","en":"I prefer coffee without sugar."}}
{"id":"volar","es":"volar","en":["to fly"],"pos":"verb","topic":"travel","note":"Stem changes: vuelo, which is also a flight.","sent":{"es":"Mañana {volamos} a Bogotá.","en":"Tomorrow we fly to Bogotá."}}
{"id":"cruzar","es":"cruzar","en":["to cross"],"pos":"verb","topic":"out","sent":{"es":"{Cruza} la calle con cuidado.","en":"Cross the road carefully."}}
{"id":"doblar","es":"doblar","en":["to turn","to fold"],"pos":"verb","topic":"out","note":"For a corner: dobla a la derecha. Also to fold clothes.","sent":{"es":"{Dobla} a la izquierda en la esquina.","en":"Turn left at the corner."}}
{"id":"celebrar","es":"celebrar","en":["to celebrate"],"pos":"verb","topic":"leisure","sent":{"es":"Vamos a {celebrar} tu cumpleaños.","en":"We are going to celebrate your birthday."}}
{"id":"pelear","es":"pelear","en":["to fight","to argue"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"Covers both a fight and a row.","sent":{"es":"No quiero {pelear} contigo.","en":"I do not want to argue with you."}}
{"id":"enamorarse","es":"enamorarse","en":["to fall in love"],"pos":"verb","topic":"feelings","note":"enamorarse de alguien.","sent":{"es":"Se {enamoró} de una colombiana.","en":"He fell in love with a Colombian woman."}}
{"id":"servir","es":"servir","en":["to serve","to be useful"],"pos":"verb","topic":"verbs","note":"Stem changes: sirve. ¿para qué sirve? is what is it for?","sent":{"es":"¿Para qué {sirve} esto?","en":"What is this for?"}}
{"id":"funcionar","es":"funcionar","en":["to work"],"pos":"verb","topic":"tech","note":"For machines and plans. A person working is trabajar.","sent":{"es":"El wifi no {funciona}.","en":"The wifi is not working."}}
{"id":"desayunar","es":"desayunar","en":["to have breakfast"],"pos":"verb","topic":"food","sent":{"es":"¿Ya {desayunaste}?","en":"Have you had breakfast yet?"}}
{"id":"almorzar","es":"almorzar","en":["to have lunch"],"pos":"verb","topic":"food","note":"Stem changes: almuerzo, which is also lunch itself.","sent":{"es":"{Almorzamos} a la una.","en":"We have lunch at one."}}
{"id":"cenar","es":"cenar","en":["to have dinner"],"pos":"verb","topic":"food","sent":{"es":"¿Dónde quieres {cenar}?","en":"Where do you want to have dinner?"}}
{"id":"cobrar","es":"cobrar","en":["to charge"],"pos":"verb","topic":"paying","note":"For a price. Charging a phone is cargar.","sent":{"es":"¿Cuánto me {cobra}?","en":"How much do you charge?"}}
{"id":"escalar","es":"escalar","en":["to climb"],"pos":"verb","topic":"leisure","note":"For rock and mountains. Climbing stairs is subir.","sent":{"es":"Los sábados vamos a {escalar}.","en":"On Saturdays we go climbing."}}
